By purchasing from or otherwise dealing with Preown, the customer agrees to:
- These Terms & Conditions;
- Applicable Return & Replacement Policy;
- Applicable Warranty Policy;
- Shipping & Delivery Policy;
- Privacy Policy; and
- Any other terms specifically communicated for the relevant product, service or transaction.

They apply to every purchase or transaction made through Preown, including purchases completed:
- Online;
- Offline;
- Through social media;
- Through WhatsApp;
- Through telephone;
- Through direct customer enquiries;
- Through Preown employees or representatives;
- At a Preown physical store;
- Through delivery/order arrangements; or
- Through any other authorized Preown sales channel.

A pre-owned device may have:
- Minor scratches;
- Minor marks;
- Signs of previous use;
- Cosmetic wear;
- Battery capacity below that of a new device; or
- Other minor imperfections consistent with its stated condition.

Before sale, Preown may inspect and test devices, including:
- Display and touchscreen;
- Cameras;
- Speakers and microphones;
- Charging functionality;
- Buttons;
- Face ID/Touch ID where applicable;
- Battery condition;
- Wi-Fi/Bluetooth;
- Cellular/network functionality;
- IMEI/serial number;
- Activation Lock/security status;
- Physical condition; and
- Other relevant hardware or software functions.

Prices displayed or communicated by Preown may change due to:
- Market conditions;
- Product availability;
- Inventory changes;
- Promotional offers;
- Supplier/seller pricing;
- Tax changes; or
- Pricing/listing errors.

Orders may be subject to:
- Product availability;
- Payment verification;
- Customer/order verification;
- Fraud and risk checks; and
- Final confirmation by Preown.

Preown may cancel or reject a transaction where:
- The product is unavailable;
- There is an apparent pricing or listing error;
- Payment cannot be verified;
- Fraudulent or suspicious activity is suspected;
- Incorrect product information was provided; or
- The transaction violates applicable law or these Terms.

Preown may accept payment through:
- UPI;
- Credit/debit cards;
- Net banking;
- Payment gateways;
- EMI/financing options;
- Bank transfer; or
- Other payment methods made available by Preown.

Delivery timelines may vary depending on:
- Location;
- Courier availability;
- Weather;
- Public holidays;
- Logistics disruptions;
- Natural events;
- Government restrictions; or
- Other circumstances beyond Preown's reasonable control.

The video should clearly show:
- Package condition;
- Shipping label/order details;
- All seals/tape;
- Opening of the package;
- Product being removed;
- Product condition;
- IMEI/serial number where visible; and
- Accessories/items received.

Inspection may include verification of:
- Product model and configuration;
- IMEI/serial number;
- Physical condition;
- Functional condition;
- Display and hardware;
- Accessories/items originally supplied;
- Physical or liquid damage;
- Tampering;
- Unauthorized repair;
- Product mismatch/device switching; and
- Compliance with the applicable return/replacement policy.

A return, refund or replacement may be rejected where inspection establishes that:
- The returned product is different from the product sold;
- IMEI/serial number does not match;
- The product has been intentionally damaged;
- The product has been opened or repaired without authorization;
- Liquid damage is found;
- Required accessories/items are missing;
- The product has been materially altered;
- The request is outside the applicable return period; or
- The claim otherwise fails to meet the applicable policy.

A return/replacement request for a new/sealed product may be considered where:
- The product is physically damaged during delivery;
- Physical damage is discovered while opening the sealed package;
- The package/product shows qualifying transit damage; or
- Another qualifying issue is established under the applicable policy or law.

The video should begin before opening the package and clearly show:
- All sides of the unopened package;
- Shipping label;
- Package seals;
- Opening of the package;
- Product being removed;
- Product condition immediately after opening;
- IMEI/serial number where visible; and
- All accessories/items received.

If a new/sealed product is found to have physical damage while opening the package or immediately after opening the seal, the customer must:
1. Stop using the product;
2. Preserve the product and packaging in the condition received;
3. Immediately contact Preown;
4. Provide the mandatory unboxing video; and
5. Provide photographs or other supporting evidence where requested.

Manufacturer warranty may exclude:
- Physical damage;
- Accidental damage;
- Liquid damage;
- Unauthorized repair;
- Misuse; and
- Other exclusions specified by the manufacturer.

The warranty does not ordinarily cover:
- Physical damage;
- Accidental damage;
- Liquid/water damage;
- Broken or cracked screens;
- Bent or heavily damaged devices;
- Unauthorized repair or opening;
- Internal component tampering;
- Altered/removed/damaged IMEI or serial number;
- Damage caused by misuse or negligence;
- Normal cosmetic wear;
- Scratches, dents or marks;
- Software issues caused by third-party applications;
- Data loss;
- Accessories unless specifically covered; or
- Damage caused after delivery through improper use.

Products purchased additionally with a device, including but not limited to:
- Phone/tablet cases;
- Tempered glass/screen protectors;
- Screen guards;
- Covers; and
- Other similar add-on accessories;

Before returning or submitting a device, customers should remove:
- Apple ID/iCloud accounts;
- Google accounts;
- Samsung or other manufacturer accounts;
- Device passwords/passcodes;
- Find My/Activation Lock;
- Other security locks; and
- Personal/confidential information.

Preown may refuse to purchase, accept, process, sell, return or warranty a device where there is reasonable evidence of:
- Theft;
- Fraud;
- Ownership dispute;
- Invalid/altered IMEI or serial number;
- Activation Lock;
- Security lock;
- Counterfeit components;
- Tampering; or
- Other unlawful activity.

Where Preown provides a trade-in or sell-your-device service, the final offer may depend upon:
- Device model;
- Storage/configuration;
- Physical condition;
- Functional condition;
- Battery condition;
- IMEI/serial verification;
- Ownership documentation;
- Market value; and
- Inspection results.

Preown may facilitate:
- Product discovery;
- Seller verification;
- Order processing;
- Payment;
- Logistics;
- Customer support; and/or
- Warranty/return handling,
depending on the transaction.

Preown may suspend, cancel or refuse transactions where it reasonably suspects:
- Payment fraud;
- Identity misuse;
- Device switching;
- False warranty claims;
- False damage claims;
- IMEI/serial manipulation;
- Abuse of return/replacement policies;
- Multiple fraudulent accounts; or
- Other fraudulent or unlawful activity.

Unless expressly stated otherwise:
- Offers cannot be combined;
- Offers cannot be exchanged for cash;
- Offers may apply only to selected products/customers;
- Offers may have validity periods; and
- Preown may withdraw an offer where permitted by law.

All Preown content, including:
- Logos;
- Brand names;
- Text;
- Product descriptions;
- Graphics;
- Photographs;
- Videos;
- Designs;
- Software;
- Website layout; and
- Other original content

Customers must not:
- Use Preown platforms for unlawful purposes;
- Attempt unauthorized access;
- Interfere with website/platform security;
- Introduce malicious software;
- Scrape or commercially copy website content without permission;
- Create fraudulent accounts;
- Submit false information; or
- Abuse any payment, promotional, return or warranty system.

Preown may use third-party services including:
- Payment gateways;
- Courier/logistics providers;
- Financing/EMI providers;
- Technology providers;
- Analytics providers; and
- Communication platforms.

This may include loss of:
- Data;
- Business;
- Profits;
- Revenue;
- Goodwill; or
- Other consequential losses.

Preown will not be responsible for failure or delay caused by circumstances beyond its reasonable control, including:
- Natural disasters;
- Floods;
- Fire;
- Epidemics/pandemics;
- War;
- Riots;
- Government restrictions;
- Strikes;
- Transportation disruptions;
- Internet/telecommunications failures; or
- Other events beyond reasonable control.

Customers may be required to provide:
- Order ID;
- Invoice;
- Registered mobile number;
- Product details;
- IMEI/serial number; and
- Supporting photographs/videos/documents.
